  "question": {
    "text": "A series <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> circuit containing an inductor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>20</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi>mH</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> a capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>120</mn><mtext>&#160;&#956;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and a resistor <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is driven by an <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> source of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>50</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi>Hz</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The energy dissipated in the circuit in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.17</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
